import json,html,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;e=html.escape
parts=['''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>ABAP from random weights: experiment results</title><style>body{max-width:1100px;margin:48px auto;padding:0 24px;background:#f7f5f1;color:#27272b;font:17px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}h1{font-size:38px;line-height:1.15}h2{margin-top:40px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}td,th{border:1px solid #d8d1c8;padding:12px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#e9e3d9}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:white;padding:18px;font:14px/1.55 ui-monospace,monospace}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;padding:10px}details{border-bottom:1px solid #d8d1c8}.note{padding:18px;border-left:4px solid #965446;background:#eee6dc}.label{color:#824639;font-weight:700}a{color:#754333}small{color:#666}</style><p class="label">WEIGHT-SPACE EXPERIMENT · 6 NOVEMBER 2026</p><h1>From random weights to ABAP recall.<br>Expert understanding: not achieved.</h1><p>Qwen3.5-0.8B's text architecture was initialized randomly (752,393,024 parameters). No pretrained neural weights were loaded. The existing tokenizer and architecture configuration were reused. All experiments disabled autograd and used no optimizer.</p><div class="note"><b>The best direct-memory edit reproduces all seven reference answers exactly.</b> That exact-recall variant still fails on the ten different-phrasing and transfer probes. A looser variant recovers one complete paraphrase answer; see the qualitative review for transfer results. This is installed memory, not demonstrated expert understanding. Narrow failures here do not prove that all possible weight-space programming methods must fail.</div>''']
parts.append('<h2>25 edit variants · 397 completed outputs</h2><p>Best reference recall: <b>7/7</b>, direct_memory/memory_95. Best fully correct development-transfer result: <b>1/10</b>, refined_memory/refined_88. These are different variants; there is no model achieving both scores as a combined result. <a href="review.json">Qualitative assessment and partial-credit notes</a>.</p><h2>Iterations</h2><table><tr><th>Method / variant</th><th>Exact reference recall</th><th>Generalization</th></tr><tr><td>Four vocabulary / residual edits</td><td>Not tested for memorization</td><td>0/7 ABAP prerequisite tasks; 0/1 language sanity task</td></tr>')
summary=[];allruns=[]
for folder in ['direct_memory','uniform_memory','expanded_memory','refined_memory','affine_memory','soft_memory']:
    f=R/folder/'memory_results.json'
    if not f.exists():continue
    rows=json.loads(f.read_text());bank=json.loads((f.parent/'memory_reference.json').read_text())
    for v in dict.fromkeys(x['variant'] for x in rows):
        group=[x for x in rows if x['variant']==v]
        recall=[x for x in group if x['id'].startswith('memorized_')]
        exact=sum(x['text'].strip()==bank[int(x['id'].split('_')[1])][1] for x in recall)
        probes=[x for x in group if not x['id'].startswith('memorized_')]
        # Semantic assessments are supplied separately after human/assistant inspection.
        entry={'folder':folder,'variant':v,'reference_exact':exact,'reference_count':len(recall),'probe_count':len(probes)}
        summary.append(entry);allruns.append((folder,v,group,bank))
        parts.append(f'<tr><td>{e(folder)} / {e(v)}</td><td>{exact}/{len(recall)}</td><td>{len(probes)} probe outputs preserved below; qualitative review</td></tr>')
parts.append('</table><h2>What was actually written?</h2><ol><li><b>Vocabulary bias:</b> sparse residual directions and amplified ABAP token rows. These changed token selection but did not create coherent language.</li><li><b>Direct associative memory:</b> reserve a constant residual coordinate; capture the final MLP input while reading each supplied answer; write those vectors into explicit gated prototype detectors; write the desired next-token embedding directions into their output columns. Unused final MLP neurons are zeroed. No loss is minimized and no optimizer runs. These are supervised reference-based memory writes, not zero-data discovery.</li><li><b>Attention rewrite:</b> analytically replace random residual transformations with a uniform-attention context average. This caused prototype collisions and failed to recall the examples.</li><li><b>Smooth similarity kernel:</b> SiLU(z) multiplied by z at negative similarity scores approximates an exponential weighting. This recovers fragments on some probes but produces malformed code and incomplete answers.</li><li><b>Explicit affine detectors:</b> add 7,168 gate/up bias parameters to the final MLP and use normalized-key similarities. This deliberately changes the architecture, and is separate from the pure existing-weight edits.</li><li><b>Reference expansion:</b> add three alternate phrasings for each of seven reference answers (28 question–answer pairs). This preserves recall at strong thresholds but does not establish semantic transfer.</li></ol><p>The seven reference answers include six ABAP explanations/code examples and one basic variable definition. Exact recall is computed automatically against these supplied strings. It must not be interpreted as a coding benchmark score.</p>')
parts.append('<h2>Limits and evaluation integrity</h2><p>The first stage has seven basic ABAP tasks and one language sanity check. Later stages use seven reference recall prompts plus ten paraphrase, contrasting-case, code-renaming, sign-change, and combined-question probes. The probes were not passed to the weight-writing code, but their outputs were inspected while choosing later methods; they are development probes, not a blind final benchmark. No SAP compiler or independent expert judge was used. The desired expert-level target remains unmet.</p><p>A generation-stop configuration bug in an early memory trial caused answers to continue after the EOS token. It was corrected before the completed memory runs. Those preliminary outputs and an earlier failed attention rewrite are retained separately and excluded from the summary. No outputs have been rewritten to improve appearances.</p>')
parts.append('<h2>All completed memory outputs</h2>')
for folder,v,rows,bank in allruns:
    parts.append(f'<details><summary>{e(folder)} / {e(v)} — {len(rows)} outputs</summary>')
    for x in rows:
        kind='Reference recall' if x['id'].startswith('memorized_') else 'Generalization probe'
        parts.append(f'<h3>{e(kind)} · {e(x["id"])}</h3><p>{e(x["prompt"])}</p><pre>{e(x["text"])}</pre>')
    parts.append('</details>')
parts.append('<h2>Original random / vocabulary outputs</h2>')
for x in json.loads((R/'results.json').read_text()):
    parts.append(f'<details><summary>{e(x["condition"])} · {e(x["test_id"])}</summary><p>{e(x["prompt"])}</p><pre>{e(x["text"])}</pre></details>')
parts.append('<h2>Files and sources</h2><p><a href="README.txt">Reproduction and usage</a> · <a href="summary.json">Machine-readable recall counts</a> · <a href="memory_attempt.py">Memory-writing code</a> · <a href="run_memory.py">Saved-memory runner</a></p><p>Reference criteria checked against SAP documentation: <a href="https://help.sap.com/docs/SUPPORT_CONTENT/abap/3353526117.html">FOR ALL ENTRIES</a>, <a href="https://help.sap.com/saphelp_gbt10/helpdata/en/fc/eb35de358411d1829f0000e829fbfe/content.htm">table categories</a>, <a href="https://help.sap.com/saphelp_ewm900/helpdata/en/fc/eb3605358411d1829f0000e829fbfe/content.htm">field-symbol row access</a>, <a href="https://help.sap.com/saphelp_SNC700_ehp01/helpdata/en/fc/eb373d358411d1829f0000e829fbfe/content.htm">binary search</a>, <a href="https://help.sap.com/docs/ABAP_PLATFORM_NEW/8132142fd1a144a59303663a03a7c2d4/b8c77e052c304bfda563dae1b89fc109.html">duplicate deletion</a>.</p></html>')
(R/'comparison.html').write_text(''.join(parts));(R/'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))
print(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))
